{"name":"Grey Porcelain","hex":"#86837a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"porcelain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard white translucent ceramic, originally made by firing kaolin, quartz, and feldspar at high temperatures but now also inclusive of similar artificial materials; also often  such a material as a symbol of the fragility, elegance, etc. traditionally associated with porcelain goods.","Synonym of china: porcelain tableware."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To coat with a porcelain enamel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porcelain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Porcelain","blocks":[{"text":"Porcelain, also called china, is a ceramic material made by heating raw materials, generally including kaolinite, in a kiln to temperatures between 1,200 and 1,400 °C. The greater strength and translucence of porcelain, relative to other types of pottery, arise mainly from vitrification and the formation of the mineral mullite within the body at these high temperatures. End applications include tableware, decorative ware such as figurines, and products in technology and industry such as electrical insulators and laboratory ware."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/%E6%B1%9D%E7%AA%AF_%E9%9D%92%E7%93%B7%E8%86%BD%E7%93%B6.png/330px-%E6%B1%9D%E7%AA%AF_%E9%9D%92%E7%93%B7%E8%86%BD%E7%93%B6.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porcelain","wikidata":"Q130693"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg/120px-Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg/250px-Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg/120px-Allegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAllegorie_van_de_herfst_-_onbekend_-_KU_Leuven_Kunstpatrimonium_-_SPK379.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/ChelseaSwanTureeen.JPG/120px-ChelseaSwanTureeen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/ChelseaSwanTureeen.JPG/250px-ChelseaSwanTureeen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/ChelseaSwanTureeen.JPG/120px-ChelseaSwanTureeen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik